  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "NameRecord::copy",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-name-table.hh",
    "description": "NameRecord::copy uses untrusted name-table fields directly (`offset` and `length`) to copy string bytes: `out->offset.serialize_copy(c, src_base + offset, dst_base, length)`. During subsetting (`name::serialize`), records are copied without re-sanitizing per-record bounds, so a malformed NameRecord whose `offset+length` exceeds the source string pool causes `UnsizedArrayOf::copy` -> `hb_array_t::copy` to read past the source allocation (ASan heap-buffer-overflow at hb-array.hh:195). Root cause is missing bounds validation of NameRecord string slice before copy, not the low-level array copy loop itself.",
    "conditions": "Trigger with a font containing a `name` table where table-level checks pass (struct/array/range), but at least one selected NameRecord has inconsistent `length`/`offset` relative to the string storage area. In hb-subset-fuzzer flow, input is loaded as a face, `hb_subset` calls `OT::name::subset` -> `name::serialize`, which iterates filtered NameRecords and calls `NameRecord::copy`; crafted `offset`/`length` makes `src_base + offset` point near/after pool end and `length` forces out-of-bounds read during byte copy."
  },
